    "https://careers.smu.edu.sg/": {
      "title": "An employer of choice, in the heart of the city",
      "description": "Home | Careers@SMU - Working In Singapore Management University Office of Human Resources Menu Careers@SMU Main navigation Home Job Openings Faculty Recruitment Professional Appointments Research Appointments Benefits & Welfare Learning & Development Employee Engagement An employer of choice, in the heart of the city Discover the reasons why SMU is such a good place to work. Find out more Join SMU as a Presidential Early Career Professor Embark on a journey of academic excellence and impact. Read More » Distinctive Interactive Pedagogy SMU is known for how our faculty hone the students' critical thinking and communication skills. Read More » WHY JOIN SMU? The ‘family-like’ atmosphere among the SMU community fosters a culture where employees work, plan, organise and play together – building a strong collegiality and morale within the university. Elvin Lim Dean, College of Integrative Studies, Professor of Political Science, Director, Wee Kim Wee Centre \"SMU is a special, vibrant place. Here, in the heart of the city, our staff, faculty and students are taking on the puzzles and challenges of the future with courage and zest. It is my privilege to be a part of this collective endeavour to touch the lives around us.\" Wang Heli Dean, College of Graduate of Research Studies Janice Bellace Professor of Strategic Management Lee Kong Chian School of Business \"Supportive funding and staff that facilitate research productivity; Dedicated students and positive classroom environment make me enjoy teaching and interacting with students.\" David Lo OUB Chair Professor of Computer Science School of Computing and Information Systems \"SMU has helped me to learn how to give an interactive lecture, design course materials, create assessments, mentor students, etc.\" Alvin See Wei Liang Associate Professor of Law Yong Pung How School of Law \"Teaching and research at SMU are conducted in a friendly and conducive environment. This fosters a close-knit academic community, much like a small family.\" Monit Sharma Research Engineer School of Computing and Information Systems \"Working at SMU has been a genuinely rewarding experience — the supportive culture makes collaboration feel natural and energizing. I’m proud to be part of SMU’s budding quantum computing research, where access to cutting edge resources and interdisciplinary teamwork help turn ideas into real impact. I especially enjoy working alongside passionate colleagues and mentor, and seeing our research translate into practical solutions every day.\" Yang Zhou Senior Research Engineer Research Lab for Intelligent Software Engineering \"Working at SMU has been a highly rewarding experience, largely due to its collaborative and supportive working environment. The university promotes intellectual freedom, allowing me to freely explore meaningful research topics aligned with my interests. The open and cooperative atmosphere among colleagues has significantly enriched my growth both personally and professionally.\" Gilbert Ong Deputy Lead, Sales, Marketing and Communications Cluster SMU Academy \"At SMU, I have the opportunity to collaborate with diverse stakeholders to achieve the shared goal of delivering comprehensive, high-quality short courses to adult learners. These courses are designed to equip learners with the skills they need to succeed in today’s workforce. My passion for helping learners meet their objectives has resulted in positive feedback from both the learners themselves and their employers.\" Ivy Wong Assistant Director Office of Advancement \"One of the greatest perks of working on campus is the access to lifelong learning opportunities—from public lectures and guest speakers to roadshows and masterclasses. At SMU, I’m surrounded by supportive colleagues who share a common mission: making a meaningful impact on our students, alumni, and the wider community. As an SMU alumna, it fills me with immense joy and pride to witness the university’s growth and contribute to its continued evolution.\" Shameem Nilofar University Librarian SMU Libraries \"No idea is too big if you are keen to create meaningful impact.  That’s the shared DNA of the dynamic core of SMU – its faculty, students, and staff. I continue to remain amazed by the agility and the creativity but also the humanity and empathy with which SMU continues to thrive in a rapidly changing world.\" CURRENT JOB OPENINGS Professional & Research Appointments See all available job openings » Faculty Appointments Full-time Faculty Job Openings » Associated Faculty Job Openings » Learn More about Overseas Postgraduate Scholarships (OPS) » Overseas Post-Doctoral Fellowships (OPF) » Early Career Award (ECA) » Where to find us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University Administration Building 81 Victoria Street Singapore 188065 Location Maps & Directions Carpark Information Terms of Use Website Feedback Report Whistleblowing Personal Data Protection Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn YouTube SoundCloud TikTok © 2026 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved. sfy39587stp30 75 80 1531 Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Back Button Back Vendor Search Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm My Choices By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. You can change your cookies settings at any time. See all website cookies Cookies Settings Accept All Cookies PageAssist Discover your personalization options"
