    "https://law.smu.edu.sg/about/careers/academic_appointments_I": {
      "title": "Academic Appointments",
      "description": "Academic Appointments | Yong Pung How School of Law Yong Pung How School of Law Search Menu Main navigation Home About Dean's Welcome About SMU YPHSL Advisory Board Distinguished Fellows Faculty Careers Annual Reports Programmes Bachelor of Laws SMU LLB–Melbourne LLM Dual Degree Bachelor of Science (Computing & Law) J.D. Programme Master of Laws (LLM) PhD in Law, Commerce and Technology LLB Admissions Student Activities Overview Moots ADR Competitions Internship Global Exposure Student Research Papers Dean's List Awards Student Clubs Pro Bono Centre SMU Law Academy Research Overview Research Cluster Awards, Prizes and Honours Research Grants Alumni Giving Contact us Breadcrumb Home About Careers Academic Appointments Dean's Welcome About SMU YPHSL Advisory Board Distinguished Fellows Faculty Careers Presidential Early Career Professorship Academic Appointments Adjunct Appointments Yong Pung How Junior Fellowship Visiting Scholars Programme Annual Reports Jump to Page Dean's Welcome About SMU YPHSL Advisory Board Distinguished Fellows Faculty Careers Presidential Early Career Professorship Academic Appointments Adjunct Appointments Yong Pung How Junior Fellowship Visiting Scholars Programme Annual Reports Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors The Singapore Management University (SMU) Yong Pung How School of Law invites scholars to apply for Professors/Associate Professors/Assistant Professors on tenure-track.  We also have a few positions on the non-tenure track and encourage applicants with the right fit to apply. A premier university in Asia, SMU is internationally recognised for its world-class research and distinguished teaching. Established in 2000, SMU's mission is to generate high impact research and to produce broad-based, creative, and entrepreneurial leaders for the knowledge-based economy.  SMU's education is known for its highly interactive, collaborative, and project-based approach to learning. The Yong Pung How School of Law is among SMU’s eight schools and colleges, offering LL.B., J.D., LL.M. and Ph.D. degrees. Located in Singapore’s Central Business District, SMU Yong Pung How School of Law has forged strong cooperation with leading law firms, courts, government agencies, multinational corporations and technology companies. Its academic research focuses on cutting-edge issues with particular focus on transnational commercial law, law and technology, dispute resolution and sustainability.  The Yong Pung How School of Law currently has over 50 faculty members and more than 800 undergraduate and postgraduate students. Our faculty members have diverse experiences in multiple jurisdictions and have published widely in leading international journals. Academic Positions (Tenure-Track) Applicants for Professorship should have an excellent publication record and international recognition in research and legal education. Success in obtaining and managing significant research grants is advantageous. For Associate Professorship, applicants should be mid-career scholars with a record of sustained excellence in both research and teaching. For Assistant Professorship, applicants should be early-career scholars who have a strong academic record and clear potential for achieving excellence in both research and teaching. Typically, the first contract is for a four-year period and Assistant Professors must undergo a mandatory tenure review before the end of the second contract which is for three years. Those with more experience may be offered only one four-year contract during which mandatory tenure review must be completed. Applicants are normally expected to have at least three substantive publications (published or accepted for publication) in leading peer-reviewed international academic journals. Academic Positions (non-tenure track) Non-tenure track faculty play a vital role in contributing to teaching, research and service.  They shoulder a greater responsibility for teaching.  Successful applicants will be appointed to the ranks of Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Principal Lecturer, Senior Lecturer or Lecturer as is commensurate with their qualifications, achievements and experience, with renewable fixed-term contracts lasting up to five years and the possibility of conversion to an open contract for high performers who have completed at least one term at SMU. We have a limited number of vacancies avialble on the non-tenure track. We invite applications for the following tracks on the non-tenure track: Practice Track faculty conduct practice-oriented or applied research, disseminating industry-relevant knowledge to private and public sector organisations. Education Track faculty engage in education-related and pedagogical research, demonstrating scholarly contributions that enhance teaching methodologies and content development. Lecturer Track faculty contribute to various academic programmes in SMU, leveraging their professional and academic experience to deliver courses aligned with their expertise. Academic Qualifications and Relevant Experience Applicants for all ranks and on both tracks (tenure or non-tenure) should ordinarily have a first degree in law and a postgraduate degree in law from reputable law schools. Applicants who do not possess a postgraduate degree in law are welcome to apply if they are able to demonstrate a strong publication record and relevant experience in teaching, legal practice, government, international organisations, or the judiciary. Evidence of successfully applying for external research grants and/or working in interdisciplinary research teams (where law is one of the research disciplines) will be an advantage.  Work experience in the judiciary, international organisations, law firms, technology companies, and governmental agencies will likewise be an advantage. Subject Areas We are looking for highly motivated and talented scholars who utilise a variety of research methodologies.  Subject areas of particular interest include the following: All areas of Private Law (Contract, Tort, Equity & Trusts and Property) Arbitration Law Comparative Asian Law (with particular focus on Chinese or Indonesian Law) Corporate and Securities Law Criminal Law Environmental and Energy Law Evidence and Procedure Financial Regulation and Fintech Intellectual Property Law Labour/Employment Law Law and Technology (especially in relation to Consumer Law, Competition/Antitrust Law, Cybersecurity, Ethics and Technology Governance, Labour/Employment Law, and Health Law) Maritime & Admiralty Law Private International Law We are also interested in applicants willing to teach the following subjects: Ethics and Social Responsibility Legal Research and Writing Comparative Legal Systems Compensation SMU offers a highly competitive salary in addition to medical and other benefits. Professors at all ranks are also eligible for travel and research funding. Application Procedure Interested applicants should submit: a cover letter (which should state, inter alia, the track the applicant is applying for); a detailed CV including publications; soft copies of 3 recent representative publications; a 3-5 page description of research and teaching interests; and a list of 3 referees with full contact information to lawcv@smu.edu.sg Applicants are advised to refer to the SMU Yong Pung How School of Law Annual Report . Application deadline : 25 September 2026 Applicants are reviewed (and may be interviewed) on a rolling basis, so early applications are strongly encouraged.  An applicant's willingness to engage in service activities at the school and/or University levels will be a key consideration. Other questions can be directed to Dr Adeline CHONG, Associate Dean (Faculty Matters) at adelinechong@smu.edu.sg (Please quote reference number in all correspondence:  YPHSL-PROF-2026-2027). SMU Yong Pung How School of Law is committed to building a culturally diverse educational environment; women and underrepresented minorities are strongly encouraged to apply. Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. For more information on Recruitment in SMU, please visit the Careers@SMU website: https://careers.smu.edu.sg/ Early Career Opportunities SMU, with the support of the Ministry of Education, offers various types of postgraduate development opportunities providing a range of support to promising Singaporeans at the early stages of their academic career. Singaporean candidates at the early stages of their academic career considering applying to the Yong Pung How School of Law may consider applying directly for one of the following opportunities: Overseas Postgraduate Scholarships (OPS) SMU’s Overseas Postgraduate Scholarship is a prestigious scholarship that aims to attract and encourage talented young Singaporeans to embark on an academic career by providing financial support as well as guidance and mentorship. The scholarship will provide financial support for up to five years while the selected scholars complete their overseas studies towards a LLM and/or PhD degree (or equivalent). Overseas Postdoctoral Fellowships (OPF) ​SMU's Overseas Postdoctoral Fellowship aims to provide doctoral candidates who are about to complete or have completed their studies at a local autonomous university, an opportunity to engage in mentored and advanced training and/or research at an overseas university or institute for one year. Early Career Award (ECA) The ECA provides outstanding Singaporeans who have recently completed their PhD or postdoctoral training an opportunity to enhance their teaching capabilities as well as establish a strong research portfolio before they are considered for a tenure track appointment at SMU. Awardees will hold appointment as Lecturer for a period of up to three years during which they will receive a research grant, reduced teaching load and guidance of an academic mentor.  Upon completion of the award, awardees will be considered to join SMU’s faculty as an Assistant Professor on the tenure track. Further details, as well as the eligibility criteria and application process, may be found at the following website: https://careers.smu.edu.sg/ Enquiries about either the OPS, OFS or ECA may be directed to Dr Adeline CHONG, Associate Dean (Faculty Matters) at adelinechong@smu.edu.sg . Hit enter to search or ESC to close Where to find us Yong Pung How School of Law 55 Armenian Street Singapore 179943 Footer Menu - Location Maps & Directions Carpark Information Get in touch Email: law@smu.edu.sg For Postgraduate Admissions Enquiries: Juris Doctor (J.D.) Programme Email: jd@smu.edu.sg Master of Laws (LLM) Programme Email: smullm@smu.edu.sg SMU Law Academy Email: smulawacademy@smu.edu.sg Footer Menu - Get in Touch Offices & Staff Directory Faculty Directory Library Terms of Use Website Feedback Report Whistleblowing Personal Data Protection Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn YouTube SoundCloud TikTok © 2026 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved. Top Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount